This package builds and runs Vampire, and the `vampire-worker` binary it produces
is Vampire with one extra translation unit (`worker/worker.cpp`) linked in.

    Vampire — https://github.com/vprover/vampire
    Built from https://github.com/Dragon-Hatcher/vampire-tactic-vampire, a fork
    carrying the changes that make a proof readable back: what each inference
    used its premises for, the substitutions it applied, and the steps
    clausification took.
    Vampire's licence is at https://vprover.github.io/license.html

Vampire's own build fetches two further components as submodules:

    CaDiCaL — https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical
    VIRAS — https://github.com/joe-hauns/viras

`Vampire/Preprocess.lean` follows lean-smt in how it reduces a goal to the
smallest query that states it. lean-smt is used under the Apache License 2.0.

    lean-smt — https://github.com/ufmg-smite/lean-smt
    Copyright (c) 2021-2026 by the authors listed in that project's AUTHORS file
    and their institutional affiliations.

The problems under `problems/` are not this project's work. They are test data,
each kept beside the file it was made from.

    TPTP — https://www.tptp.org, Geoff Sutcliffe. `problems/tptp/`, from
    TPTP v9.3.1.
    SMT-LIB — https://smtlib.cs.uiowa.edu. `problems/smtlib/`.
